+# Image retention under bounded database capacity — prospective local plan
+
+Allocation: `image-capacity-txn-a62f-20260922-01`. Intake and source anchor: `2308b8301d69b7089a2e0636486736ed59b61537`.
+
+## Origin, new decision, and publication chronology
+
+Closed #3876 requires recoverable content and explicit capacity; closed #717 covers bounded pending notifications, not failure while storing referenced images. The preceding conversation-local 6c29 result tests deletion/replacement AFTER successful image retention and explicitly excludes capacity. It has been restored and audited without any formal rerun. #3931/#3955 deal with process-crash split writes; #3941 with concurrent result commits; #4029/#4057 with PNG cache validation/size; none supplies this image-object storage-full/recovery comparison. Preserve those results. This is a new local-host contract decision, not an allegation that the upstream reader has a storage implementation or an SQLite defect.
+
+GitHub currently reports #3876 CLOSED, closed_at 2026-09-21T20:10:34Z. Do not describe it as open or reopen it. Its prior plan text is not changed. Global research acceptance remains unestablished regardless of tracker state.
+
+GitHub MCP in this session exposes 48 read operations, no issue/commit/PR/merge write action. Plugin discovery found the existing GitHub integration, not an additional write route. The provided container has no gh/Docker CLI, no GH_TOKEN/GITHUB_TOKEN, and no configured Git credential helper. This is a local capability limitation, NOT the user's repository permission, a fleet-wide failure or a new research question. This source/gate registration is LOCAL and precedes formal execution, not a public GitHub preregistration. The remote branch and successor Issue remain uncreated.
+
+## H — falsifiable hypothesis
+
+For the same two pending notification records and exact image bytes, committing notification metadata/cursor before object storage may strand one or two missing images when the private database reaches its page limit. A host that puts the complete notification page, exact verified image bytes and cursor in one transaction should retain either the prior complete prefix or the new complete prefix. After one explicitly declared capacity increase and a fresh read FROM THE SAVED CURSOR, the atomic policy should retain both images; metadata-first should read no pending page and still lack the failed images. Source bytes remain available; this is not permanent data loss.
+
+No new action is executed or replayed. Both policies must report native storage failure, not fabricated success. This study tests recoverability through a specified saved-cursor path, not whether a different specialized repair could recover metadata-first state.
+
+## Analytical reduction
+
+The invariant is that every image digest referenced by the host's retained notification prefix has its exact verified bytes in the same host store. Initially one notification and its image establish this invariant. In the atomic policy, no new prefix is visible until the transaction commits all metadata, both images and cursor. If it commits, the invariant holds for all three notifications. If a statement fails and the transaction is rolled back, the original prefix and image remain and the invariant holds for that prefix. The implementation inspects transaction state and explicitly rolls back if it is still active; it does not assume every SQLite error auto-rolls back.
+
+In the comparator, the first metadata commit already exposes new image references and cursor while their BLOB writes are still uncommitted. A later object-storage failure cannot undo an earlier committed transaction. Under its registered generic saved-cursor recovery, those already-read notifications will not be fetched again. This is a known transactional-design boundary. The experiment resolves the actual engine-error, partial-image stage, preserved prior state, process exit and recovery behavior; it is not new database theory.
+
+## T — exact finite test
+
+Environment: provided Linux x86_64 execution container; CPython3.13.5, SQLite3.46.1, ordinary private regular files, DELETE journal, synchronous=FULL, 4096-byte pages, one writer per case. No Docker/OrbStack image attestation, no installs, GUI/input, model/provider, experimental network, user data or shared-runtime change. Private database capacity only; never fill the host filesystem.
+
+Exact original reader/CLI/DeliveryLedger source bytes are copied unchanged and Git-blob verified in SOURCE_BINDINGS.json. A bounded fixture uses actual DeliveryLedger.prepare for three generated RGB PNG notifications. The actual module CLI first reads one notification; that page/cursor/image initializes the store. It then reads the two pending notifications. An exec'd host validates and captures the exact image bytes before storing. The independent observer opens the database read-only after the host exits. The source images and stream remain immutable across all phases.
+
+Policies: META_THEN_OBJECTS commits notification page/cursor first, then each image in a separate transaction. ATOMIC_PAGE puts metadata, both images and cursor in one transaction. These are explicitly authored experimental hosts, not alternative versions of production runtime. The schema intentionally does not enforce a notification-to-image foreign key: that missing-image invariant is the object of the test, not a claimed FK guarantee.
+
+Conditions: ROOM uses 64 pages. FULL_FIRST uses the INITIAL actual page_count. FULL_SECOND uses INITIAL page_count plus 10 pages, enough for image2 but not image3. Recorded construction starts at 6 pages; inputs are 16x16, 128x64 and 128x128 RGB PNGs (852,24713,49363 bytes). Final inputs across both policies and every capacity condition are byte-identical WITHIN a repetition; salts differ by phase/repetition. All PNGs must remain <=65536 bytes. No threshold adjustment after formal starts.
+
+Minimum sample: 18 cases: two policies, three conditions, three repetitions. Reps 1/2/3 are THREE separately invoked immutable six-case batches, fixed condition order ROOM/FULL_FIRST/FULL_SECOND; odd repetitions run metadata-first before atomic, even the reverse. Each subprocess gets 3s; each batch a 20s foreground supervisor deadline, below the 30s tool envelope. Every child and runner wait status and the outer shell's supervisor exit are retained. Expected STORAGE_CAPACITY workers exit 2; other processes exit 0. A scientific capacity failure is not a missing process receipt.
+
+Each case has exactly one registered recovery phase after the first result and observer snapshot: the policy's fresh worker explicitly sets max_page_count=64 and consumes a new CLI response starting at the retained cursor. If there is no pending page it performs no writes. This is the treatment's bounded storage-recovery step, not a hidden formal rerun or authorization to redispatch an application action. A final CLI tail read verifies no extra notification. No automatic retry, page replacement, case exclusion or pooling with construction/predecessors.
+
+Construction-r0 and r1 are excluded. Source matching was corrected BEFORE formal freeze and both construction sources/outcomes are retained. Construction-r1 raw audit and all10 copied-evidence mutations must pass before formal.
+
+## D — predeclared decisions
+
+PASS_IMAGE_CAPACITY_TRANSACTION_SCOPED only if all18 cases/198 subprocess receipts, three batch exits, source identities, original PNG/stream bytes and all retained database states reconcile with the independent audit. Required per repetition:
+
+- ROOM: both policies retain all3 notifications/images and exact cursor; recovery has no pending work.
+- FULL_FIRST: both hit native SQLITE_FULL code13 at the first new image. Metadata-first retains all3 notifications/cursor but only the old image. Atomic retains ONLY the old complete prefix/cursor/image.
+- FULL_SECOND: both stage the first new image and hit SQLITE_FULL at the second. Metadata-first retains image1/image2 and metadata/cursor for all3; atomic rolls back the entire new page, preserving only image1 and the old prefix/cursor.
+- Registered recovery: all atomic fault cases reread precisely the two pending notifications, retain both images exactly and have no duplicate notification/old-image corruption. Metadata-first fault cases read no pending notifications and retain their originally observed missing-image state. Do not count this as permanent or universally irrecoverable loss.
+- All prior image/response bytes unchanged, all no-authority/ACK/input flags neutral; source/row/process/database/observer reconciliation complete; ten copied-evidence mutations rejected.
+
+A complete contrary result is FAIL_IMAGE_CAPACITY_TRANSACTION_HYPOTHESIS. Missing/source/process/timeout evidence yields STOP/HOLD without scientific PASS. Expected baseline missing images remain a separate FAIL_SAVED_CURSOR_IMAGE_COMPLETENESS; the boundary-hypothesis PASS cannot make that comparator safe. A deferred first outcome is not initial success, and recovery success is labelled separately.
+
+## C / U
+
+Quiescent source capture, one trusted epoch, one writer, private SQLite BLOB store and persistent original source are explicit assumptions. No crash, power failure, true block-device ENOSPC, fsync failure, quotas on rollback journal, concurrent edits/commits, garbage collection, dedup/retention TTL, hard realtime, current GUI authority, ACK/model consumption, exactly-once task execution, performance/token or production claim. SQLite synchronous FULL is a setting, not a measured hardware durability guarantee. Two stored bytes compared by digest also undergo exact byte and PNG pixel verification.
+
+No population probability or calibrated combined standard uncertainty/coverage factor is estimated. Outcomes are exact strings, integers, bytes and process-order conditions. Monotonic nanosecond times are diagnostics, not benchmarks.
+
+## Variables and unit check
+
+| Symbol / code field | Meaning (日本語) | SI / unit | Definition | Domain / assumption | Type |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| page_size | データベース1ページの長さ | 情報量B、SI物理量ではない | SQLite PRAGMA readback; 4096B | positive fixed integer | scalar integer |
+| page_count | 使用中のページ数 | 1 (count) | SQLite PRAGMA readback | nonnegative integer | scalar integer |
+| max_page_count | 当該接続のページ上限 | 1 (count) | actual applied quota | current size or greater; <=64 | scalar integer |
+| image_bytes | 検証済み画像の長さ | B (octets), not SI physical | exact file-byte count | 1..65536 | scalar integer |
+| offset | 消費済みstreamの位置 | B (octets), not SI physical | end of complete JSONL prefix | 0..1048576 | scalar integer |
+| next_sequence | 次に読む通知の番号 | 1 (count) | cursor next record identity | 2 initially; 4 after full page | scalar integer |
+| rep | 固定反復ID | 1 | prospective repetition index | formal 1,2,3; construction separate | scalar integer |
+| started_ns / finished_ns | 同一clockの診断時刻 | s, recorded in ns | CLOCK_MONOTONIC readings | order only; not wall-clock estimates | scalar integer |
+
+Unit check: 64 pages of4096B permit262144B of database content; the6-page first cap permits24576B. These are limits on the database file, not total evidence size or physical disk occupancy. Event sequence counts are never compared to byte offsets, and nanosecond diagnostics never decide storage validity.
+
+## Bounded roadmap and stop
+
+Verified predecessor bytes -> excluded engine/capture construction -> exact local source/gate freeze -> three first-outcome batches -> separate raw-only audit and corruption controls -> additive report/source/raw/patch -> GitHub evidence PR only through a supported write path -> exact-head review/checks/main readback -> own-branch deletion only after merged evidence and dependencies checked.
+
+Publication unavailability is kept here, not a wrapper-only successor. Do not claim main integration or global ROADMAP completion. A future production decision must select a real producer/host store; this research host is not promoted automatically.
+
+Primary sources consulted: SQLite PRAGMA max_page_count (https://www.sqlite.org/pragma.html#pragma_max_page_count) and transaction error response (https://www.sqlite.org/lang_transaction.html). These document the mechanism; local raw evidence determines this allocation's result.
